I reviewed the failure. Two things are going on:

1. **Endpoint 404** – the viewer calls a dedicated `/api/analytics/decision-model-logs` route that the backend does not expose. Decision-model runs are persisted in the shared AI-log store, so the client must probe the known log routes (dedicated → generic AI-log listing) and use the first one that actually resolves.
2. **Desktop mode** – `openDecisionModelLogs()` did a raw `$router.push()`, which leaves the `/desktop` route and tears the dockview workspace down. It must go through the unified `openApp()` opener so it becomes a **tab/panel** in desktop mode (and a route only in single mode). That requires registering the viewer in the app registry + component map.

## 1. API — endpoint review (probe + fallback)

